+
+## Existing code changed, and why
+
+- `DeliveryDetails.php` – the order save refuses a customer on stop and sets `salesorders.creditheld=1` when the order takes the customer over the limit (needs `CheckCreditLimits` > 0).
+- `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php` – blocks dispatch/invoice of a held order or an order of a customer on stop (checked on load and again just before posting; credit control can release an order). BR-06 said existing orders must not ship on a stop; nothing checked this before.
+- `RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php` – skips templates of a customer on stop (template not advanced, so it is retried after release); over-limit orders are held and not auto-invoiced.
+- `EDIProcessOrders.php` – refuses orders for a customer on stop, holds over-limit ones. **I also fixed `if ($CreateOrder = true)` to `==`**: it was an assignment, so no check (mine or the existing ones) could ever stop an order. Side effect: orders with parse errors are now really not created, as the code intended.
+- `api/includes/api_salesorders.php`, `api_errorcodes.php` – the web shop/API refuses orders for a customer on stop (new error 1174 "account is on hold, contact us" so the shop can show a message instead of a silent failure, BR-11), holds over-limit orders after lines are added, and refuses to invoice a held/stopped order.
+- `api/includes/api_customers.php`, `Customers.php`, `Z_ImportDebtors.php` – new customers get a next review date. `Customers.php` now lets only users with the credit control token change the credit status or limit (others keep the stored values; fields shown read-only) and logs changes to the credit control history (BR-07, 34). **The API's `ModifyCustomer` can still change them** – it has no per-user token check; left alone.
+- `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` – copies the three new debtor columns and moves the credit control tables to the new code (otherwise the history would be orphaned).
+- `CreditStatus.php` – the two credit control records cannot be edited or deleted there (that would silently lift a stop); the list labels "watch". (The page itself still cannot create a watch record; credit control creates its own.)
+- `AgedDebtors.php` – credit status, limit and last reminder columns (BR-31).
+- `SelectCustomer.php` – status banner and links to the review and reminders pages (BR-09).
+- `Z_CheckDebtorsControl.php` – it read `chartdetails`, which update 20 dropped, so it was already broken. It now uses `gltotals` and splits invoices/credits, receipts, interest and fees, waivers, write-offs and other, and lists the entries that differ and the GL postings to debtors with no customer entry.
+
+## Decisions on the BRD's open questions
+
+1. Interest: simple annual rate (Finance sets it) charged monthly as 1/12, same rate for all currencies and countries.
+2. Late fee: one flat fee per customer per month, set in the home currency and converted at the current rate to the customer's currency.
+3. No interest on interest or fees (type 70 items are never in the base). Interest only on undisputed invoices overdue more than the "charge days"; payments on account reduce the base.
+4. Final notice does **not** auto-stop by default; a switch in the setup turns it on.
+5. Over-limit orders from every route (including web shop and standing orders) are **held**, not rejected; a customer on stop is rejected.
+6. Write-off approval threshold is a setup value in home currency (default 500, Finance to set); approval is the Finance Director's token (21). The Financial Accountant has no extra sign-off. A write-off paid later: not built – a late receipt is entered as a normal receipt on the account; Finance should decide if it needs a recovery posting.
+7. Reps see the stop/watch status and the reason text (the status description).
+8. Letters are in the wording Finance enters; no per-language letters (open question 9).
+9. Watch status is not shown in the portal (the portal page shows balance, reminders, charges only).
+10. Credit limit is per customer account (`debtorsmaster`); there is no head-office/branch group limit in webERP.
+11. Cover when both are away: access is the security token, so Finance gives the token to whoever covers.
+
+## Other choices to know about
+
+- **Ledger postings**: new transaction types 70 (interest/fee), 71 (waiver), 72 (write-off) in `systypes`, so they appear on statements and in the aged debtors report under their own names. Posting follows the usual pattern (transaction, `EnsureGLEntriesBalance` just before the commit). Waivers use the charge's own rate. Write-offs credit debtors control at the invoices' original rates, debit bad debts at today's rate and post the difference to the sales exchange difference account (BR-27). Write-offs are allocated oldest first to open items.
+- **Uniqueness**: `creditcharges` has a unique key (customer, month, type), so a month can never be charged twice even with two users. The "month" is a label chosen on the page (default current month); balances are as of today.
+- **Reminders**: one stage at a time, never the same stage twice in the current overdue episode, and not within `CreditControlDunningGap` days of the last letter. A failed email is not recorded, so the next run retries. No-email customers are shown with their letter for posting and recorded as `post`.
+- **Immutability**: `creditreviews`, `creditcontrollog` and `dunninglog` have no update or delete code anywhere.
+- **Go-live**: update 44 sets `nextreviewdate` to +12 months for all customers; the spreadsheet stop list and limits load through the CSV on `CreditControlSetup.php`, with each change logged. Status stays "normal" until loaded.
+- **Security tokens 17 and 21** are new. Seeded to roles AR Clerk (17), Accountant (17, 21) and System Administrator (17, 21); Finance must assign them to the actual credit controller/deputy/FD roles. `CreditReview.php` and `CreditControlReport.php` are visible with token 2 (reps) and read-only without token 17; `SalesmanLogin` limits a rep to their own customers on every new page.
+- The upgrade adds a numbered file, so every logged-in session is redirected to the upgrade page until an authorised user runs it (existing project behaviour).
+
+## Not done / follow-up
+
+- `CheckCreditLimits` must be set to warn or prohibit in system parameters for over-limit holds (BR-10); it is not changed by the upgrade because turning it on at go-live would hold orders for every customer still on the default 1000 limit.
+- `install/sql/demo.sql` was not regenerated; a demo install picks the schema up through update 44 on first login.
+- Old customer-code changes through the API, `ModifyCustomer` tokens, and a "recovery of written-off debt" posting are not covered.
+- Help links of the new pages point at `AccountsReceivable`; the new manual chapter is `ManualCreditControl.html`.
+- Not covered by any automated test; the repo has no harness for these pages.
