diff --git a/doc/Manual/ManualCreditControl.html b/doc/Manual/ManualCreditControl.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6049624
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/Manual/ManualCreditControl.html
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+<a id="CreditControl"><h1>Credit Control</h1></a>
+<p>
+Credit control applies the same rules to every customer on account: periodic credit reviews, a stop and watch status, overdue reminder letters, month end interest and late fees, and bad debt write-offs. Everything credit control does to a customer is kept in a history that cannot be changed, which the auditors can inspect.
+</p>
+<p>
+Credit control is done by users with the <i>Credit control</i> security token (the credit controller, the deputy and the Finance Director). Write-off approval and the credit control setup need the <i>Credit control approval and setup</i> token (the Finance Director). Sales reps and sales office staff can see the credit status but cannot change it or the credit limit.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Credit reviews</h2>
+<p>
+From the customer selection screen choose <i>Credit Status and Review</i>. The page shows the credit status, limit, balance, overdue amount and the date the next review is due. Record a review with its outcome (limit confirmed, raised, reduced, put on watch, put on stop, taken off stop or watch), the notes and the next review date. A new limit takes effect at once and is recorded with the review. Reviews are never changed or deleted. New customers get a next review date automatically, from the standard review period in the credit control setup.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Stop and watch</h2>
+<p>
+A customer on <b>stop</b> cannot have a new order accepted from any route (the sales office, counter sales, the web shop and other API clients, EDI orders and recurring orders), and goods cannot be dispatched or invoiced on orders taken before the stop. Credit control can release an individual order from the credit control report. A customer on <b>watch</b> can still be supplied, the person taking the order sees a warning, and orders taken for the customer are listed on the credit control report. The status is shown on the customer selection screen, on the customer inquiry pages, when taking an order and on the aged debtors report.
+</p>
+<p>
+Stop and watch are credit status records (Setup, Credit Status). The two records used by credit control cannot be changed or deleted on the Credit Status page.
+</p>
+<h3>Orders over the credit limit</h3>
+<p>
+When credit limit checking is switched on in the system parameters (<i>Check Credit Limits</i> set to warn or prohibit), an order that takes the customer over the credit limit is accepted but held for credit control. It cannot be dispatched or invoiced until credit control releases it from the credit control report.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Disputed invoices and exemptions</h2>
+<p>
+On the credit review page credit control can mark an open invoice as disputed. A disputed invoice is not chased and not charged interest until the dispute is cleared. A customer can also be exempted from interest and from late fees, with a reason.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Reminder letters</h2>
+<p>
+The stages (how many, the days overdue that trigger each and the wording of each letter) are set up by Finance in <i>Credit Control Setup</i>. <i>Run Overdue Reminder Letters</i> shows who will get which letter. Untick the customers to leave out of the run, for example where a payment has been promised, and press <i>Send Reminders</i>. Letters are emailed to the customer's accounts contact (the contact flagged for statements, otherwise the branch email). Customers without an email address are listed, and their letter is shown on screen to print and post. A customer moves up one stage at a time and only while still overdue, never receives the same stage twice and does not receive a letter within the minimum number of days after the last one. Every reminder is recorded with its date, stage, invoices and amount.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Month end interest and late fees</h2>
+<p>
+<i>Month End Interest and Late Fees</i> lists what will be charged to whom. Interest is one twelfth of the yearly rate on the undisputed invoices that are overdue by more than the charge days; the late fee is a flat fee, converted to the customer currency, once per customer per month. Interest and fees are never charged on earlier interest and fees. Press <i>Confirm and Post Charges</i> to raise them as separate items on the customer account (they appear on the statement as <i>Interest and Late Fee</i>) and in the general ledger. A month cannot be charged twice for a customer. A charge can be waived with a reason, which posts a credit to the customer and reverses the ledger entries.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Bad debt write-offs</h2>
+<p>
+<i>Bad Debt Write-offs</i> writes off all or part of the unpaid balance with a reason. Write-offs up to the limit set by Finance are posted at once; larger ones wait for the Finance Director's approval and nothing is posted until then. The write-off is allocated to the oldest open invoices, reduces the customer's balance and posts to the bad debt account; any exchange difference is posted to the exchange difference account. By default the customer is put on stop. The same page reports write-offs over a period with who requested and who approved each.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Credit control report</h2>
+<p>
+<i>Credit Control Report</i> (Receivables, Reports) lists the customers due or overdue for a review, the customers over their credit limit and by how much, the customers on watch or on stop, and the orders held for credit control or taken for customers on watch. It can be filtered by sales rep and currency and shows totals in the home currency. A sales rep sees only their own customers.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Customer portal</h2>
+<p>
+Customers who log in see their own balance, the reminder letters sent to them and the interest and fees charged to their account under <i>Credit Reminders and Charges</i>. They never see the watch status.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Month end reconciliation</h2>
+<p>
+<i>Debtors Control Integrity</i> (Utilities) compares the trade debtors control account in the general ledger with the customer accounts for the periods chosen, showing interest and fees, waivers and write-offs on their own, and lists the entries that differ and why.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Going live</h2>
+<p>
+On upgrade every existing customer is "normal" and gets a next review date twelve months ahead. Credit control can load the status, limit and next review date held on the old spreadsheet from <i>Credit Control Setup</i> (a CSV file: customer code, status, limit, next review date). Customers listed as stop are put on stop and the change is recorded in their history.
+</p>
+
+<h2>Note for sales staff</h2>
+<p>
+<b>Watch</b>: you can take orders for the customer, but you will see a warning, and credit control sees the order. <b>Stop</b>: the system will not accept an order for the customer and nothing is dispatched or invoiced; do not promise the customer delivery and send them to credit control. You cannot change a status or limit yourself.
+</p><!-- Help End: CreditControl -->
